"""Outlines for the children's names, baked from Floraison des Amours.

Generated once offline with fontTools + HarfBuzz + shapely, then frozen here so
generate_panel_dxf.py stays stdlib-only. Each name is ONE connected piece:
rings[0] is the outer boundary, further rings are counters and drop out.
Coordinates are mm relative to the piece's own lower-left corner, curves
flattened to 0.04 mm.

Not a stencil face, and it needs not be: the letters ARE the parts here, so a
counter is simply a hole in the part.

IMPORTANT - the letterforms are FATTENED by 0.3 mm from the typeface as drawn.
As designed, this script joins its letters with hairlines only 0.50-0.55 mm
wide. In 3 mm aluminium those are load-bearing threads: the name would arrive
as a row of letters held together by wire. The outward offset takes the
narrowest neck to about 1.1 mm while leaving the thick/thin contrast intact.
Do not remove it.

The i-dots and some flourishes do not touch the letters, so each loose part is
tied on with a short 2.5 mm weld tab.
"""

